 v2.5.3 adds: security hardening — default admin/tuxwall credentials no
 longer auto-create (fail-closed setup gate with working first-admin
 enrollment), UFW raw-rule verb whitelist, CSRF Origin check, login
 rate-limit identity spoof fix, blocklist SSRF guard, 30-minute session
 idle timeout, two-step backup restore with code-replace confirmation
 (web + single-file paths, backend snapshotted first), login rate limit
 and security headers in nginx (dual-mode Secure cookie ready for TLS);
 System page gains structured DHCP (Kea) and DNS (Unbound) config forms
 with validation and automatic rollback, themed form-field styling, an
 updates-available indicator, and cache-bust bump.
 .
 v2.5.4 adds: postinst retires any WAN-wide OpenSSH allow on upgrade when
 scoped SSH access (LAN/VPN interface rules) already exists, and only
 adds SSH/HTTP allows when missing — upgrades no longer reopen or keep
 internet-facing SSH.
 .
 v2.5.5 adds: System page gains a Traffic Shaping (CAKE SQM) card — live
 caps/status/drop counters, rate editing via /etc/tuxwall/sqm.conf, and a
 guided Ookla speedtest (shaping lifted for a clean reading, then
 restored) with ~93% suggested rates and provisioning-mismatch warnings;
 per-interface DHCP pools with multi-subnet Kea APIs, interface binding
 and validation (replacing the single-subnet DHCP Pool card); agent
 sudoers rewritten without wildcards for sudo-rs; setup.sh stamps asset
 versions so browsers never run stale dashboard JS after upgrades.
 .
